-- title:
--   Cached Gaussian-integer quadrature rule at height 132
-- statement:
--   Use the published candidate phase-correlation table and fixed-point phase pairs to define integer numerators $A_k,B_k$ by finite sums with binomial and panel-center weights. Define the common positive denominator
--
--   $$
--   D_k=16\cdot10^{200}\cdot10^{310}\cdot W\cdot8^{183}\cdot183!\cdot16^k k!,
--   $$
--
--   where $W$ is the published theta integration-weight denominator, and set
--
--   $$
--   \widetilde R_k=\frac{3^{k+1}(A_k+iB_k)}{D_k}.
--   $$
--
--   The definition also stores the proposed phase pairs. Equality with the direct rational quadrature and the phase recurrences requires separate certificates.
-- source:
--   Cached integer version of direct oscillatory quadrature based on theta/Mellin and jet work by Gabewhigham and sometik179.

/- Candidate cached Gaussian-integer form of the height-132 rule.
The theta/Mellin and jet framework is due to Gabewhigham and sometik179.
The data and formulas alone assert no equality or error bound. -/
